    isbefore: []  # 3b38
    duplicate_of: []  # 3b38
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3b38
    pr_ref:  # 3b38
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-13 by WI-tusad B6. A commit that DELETES a test file (git rm) leaves that path in smart-test's affected-test selection (.ci/affected-tests.txt listed packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/tests/test_zig_floor_stable_id.py after its git rm). The targeted run then collected 0 items (\"6 workers [0 items]\", \"no tests ran in 1.47s\"), exited 5, and printed \"COVERAGE: (all files at 100%)\": the whole 824-file run was silently skipped. Restoring the file made the same selection run 25,923 tests. Expected: deleted paths are dropped from the selection (or the run fails loudly naming them). Not investigated further: where in smart-test the selection is built from the diff."  # 3b38
    fields:  # 3b38
      statement: "A targeted smart-test run never silently collects zero tests"  # 3b38
      root_cause: "not investigated: the selection keeps a git-rm'd test path and pytest collects nothing"  # 3b38
