- op: discuss  # 592a
  at: '2026-10-13T07:58:32Z'  # 592a
  by: agent  # 592a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 592a
  clock: 4  # 592a
  nonce: 592a  # 592a
  message: "Fixed in PR #1567 (merged as 836260b4dc). Root cause: CHANGED_TEST_FILES was built from `git diff --name-only`, which names a deleted file exactly like an edited one, so a git-rm'd test entered the selection. `pytest -n` given a dead path is not a usage error under xdist (\"N workers [0 items]\", exit 5, not-found message kept in a worker), and summarize_pytest_output had no result-line pattern for \"no tests ran\", so the only verdict printed was \"COVERAGE: (all files at 100%)\". Fix (a): changed test paths are split into on-disk (selected) and deleted (named, not selected); require_selection_on_disk refuses (exit 1) a manifest or run set naming a missing path; the Woodpecker step refuses such a manifest before pytest. Fix (b): run_pytest counts executed tests from a fresh junit report; exit 5/4 or all-skipped prints \"ZERO TESTS EXECUTED\", claims no coverage, exits non-zero. Nothing-to-run stays exit 0 with its own message. Evidence on merged dev, throwaway branch, uncommitted: (1) the filed repro: `git rm packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/tests/test_zig_floor_stable_id.py` + edit tests/test_smart_test_foreign_repo.py, `pytest` -> rc=0, \"smart-test: deleted test file(s) in this change, not selected ... test_zig_floor_stable_id.py\", \"4 passed\", manifest SELECTED_TESTS = tests/test_smart_test_foreign_repo.py only (grep -c zig_floor = 0). (2) deletion only: `pytest` -> rc=0, \"smart-test: 0 tests ran - nothing affected, nothing to run: the only test-relevant change deletes test file(s): ...test_zig_floor_stable_id.py\". (3) forced zero-collect: `pytest -k no_such_test_zzz` with one edited test -> rc=5, \"no tests ran\", \"ZERO TESTS EXECUTED: this is NOT a pass (exit 5)\", no coverage section. (4) the item's dead-path-under-xdist shape: `pytest packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/tests/test_zig_floor_stable_id_DELETED.py` -> rc=5, same ZERO TESTS EXECUTED block. PR CI ran the new Woodpecker step: 134 selected files, 2258 passed, 2 skipped. Tests: tests/test_smart_test_zero_collect.py (end-to-end in a fixture repo), test_smart_test_coverage_gate.py, test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py, test_check_package_coverage.py. Analogues filed: INV-zuvij (CI passes all-skipped run), WI-kazig (deleted source module may not select its importers; unverified)."  # 592a
- op: discuss  # f65b
  at: '2026-10-14T15:51:29Z'  # f65b
  by: agent  # f65b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f65b
  clock: 5  # f65b
  nonce: f65b  # f65b
  message: "Owner decision 2026-10-14: an all-skipped targeted smart-test run keeps FAILING locally (no pass-with-warning). Rationale: a run that executed zero tests is exactly the false-green this invariant forbids; a missing optional dependency should surface as a failure, not a warning that can be missed. No code change needed; #1567 behaviour stands."  # f65b
